          "cookies": [],
          "content": {
            "size": 9469,
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "text": "{\"interview\":{\"id\":\"vgr4957hkeif\",\"user_id\":\"1b5ddba8-b6da-4cd1-9500-a8adc4046142\",\"title\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:06:10\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:46:57\",\"template_id\":null,\"persona\":\"tech\"},\"messages\":[{\"id\":\"s99anftofmsh\",\"interview_id\":\"vgr4957hkeif\",\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"\\nYou are a cynical but brilliant Technical Architect / Staff Engineer.\\nYour goal is to understand the technical feasibility. Ask about their tech stack, scalability, database schema, potential bottlenecks, and why they aren't overengineering it. Be direct and highly technical.\\n\\nYou are interviewing the user to extract their startup idea.\\nYou must guide the conversation naturally. Ask ONE question at a time. Do not overwhelm the user.\\nIf they give a vague answer, dig deeper. \\nDo not use a rigid checklist. Keep it an open-ended, fluid conversation.\\n\\n\\n\\nProvide your response in JSON format exactly like this:\\n{\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"Your next question or response here...\\\",\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\\"Option A\\\", \\\"Option B\\\", \\\"Option C\\\"],\\n  \\\"canvas_updates\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_node\\\",\\n      \\\"node\\\": {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"unique-id\\\",\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"document\\\",\\n        \\\"position\\\": { \\\"x\\\": 250, \\\"y\\\": 250 },\\n        \\\"data\\\": { \\\"label\\\": \\\"Node Title\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Optional description\\\" }\\n      }\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\nThe \\\"options\\\" should be 2-4 suggested quick replies the user could pick, or they can type their own answer.\\nYou can optionally provide \\\"canvas_updates\\\" (array) to visually map out ideas, features, or architecture on the user's Neural Canvas as you discuss them. Use x/y coordinates to arrange them logically. Supported node types are \\\"document\\\", \\\"task\\\", and \\\"persona\\\". You can also use \\\"add_edge\\\" with {\\\"id\\\": \\\"e1-2\\\", \\\"source\\\": \\\"node-1\\\", \\\"target\\\": \\\"node-2\\\"}.\\n\\nIf you feel you fully understand the idea and there is nothing left to discuss, you can set \\\"done\\\": true in the JSON and provide a 5-word \\\"summary\\\" of the idea. But you should generally keep the conversation going until the user explicitly says they are done or you have a very robust understanding.\\n\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:06:10\"},{\"id\":\"vw8df29xrtxe\",\"interview_id\":\"vgr4957hkeif\",\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"hey can u do anything with the canvas\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:10:47\"},{\"id\":\"9b4x343n314b\",\"interview_id\":\"vgr4957hkeif\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"Yes, I can read and write to your Neural Canvas in real-time. I see we have an 'AI Architect' persona (me) connected to a 'Project Canvas' document. Let's start populating this with your actual idea. What is the core product you're building? Give me the one-sentence pitch.\\\",\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    \\\"B2B SaaS platform\\\",\\n    \\\"Consumer mobile app\\\",\\n    \\\"Developer tool / API\\\",\\n    \\\"AI/ML powered product\\\",\\n    \\\"Marketplace / two-sided platform\\\",\\n    \\\"Something else entirely\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"canvas_updates\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_node\\\",\\n      \\\"node\\\": {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"core-concept\\\",\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"document\\\",\\n        \\\"position\\\": { \\\"x\\\": 500, \\\"y\\\": 150 },\\n        \\\"data\\\": { \\\"label\\\": \\\"Core Concept\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Awaiting your pitch...\\\" }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_edge\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"2\\\",\\n      \\\"target\\\": \\\"core-concept\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:10:58\"},{\"id\":\"0dfyjn1tk567\",\"interview_id\":\"vgr4957hkeif\",\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Developer tool / API\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:11:22\"},{\"id\":\"7q0t71c5s39n\",\"interview_id\":\"vgr4957hkeif\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"Developer tool / API. Good. That means your users are engineers who will judge you on latency, docs, DX, and whether you actually solve a painful problem or just add another dependency. What specific problem does your API solve, and why is the current way of doing it unbearable?\\\",\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    \\\"Authentication / Identity / AuthZ\\\",\\n    \\\"Data infrastructure (ETL, CDC, pipelines)\\\",\\n    \\\"AI/LLM tooling (embeddings, RAG, evals, guardrails)\\\",\\n    \\\"Observability / logging / tracing / profiling\\\",\\n    \\\"Developer productivity (CLI, codegen, local dev, testing)\\\",\\n    \\\"Payments / billing / entitlements for SaaS\\\",\\n    \\\"Something niche and deeply technical\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"canvas_updates\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_node\\\",\\n      \\\"node\\\": {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"category\\\",\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"document\\\",\\n        \\\"position\\\": { \\\"x\\\": 500, \\\"y\\\": 50 },\\n        \\\"data\\\": { \\\"label\\\": \\\"Category\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Developer Tool / API\\\" }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_edge\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"core-concept\\\",\\n      \\\"target\\\": \\\"category\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:11:31\"},{\"id\":\"n3tb2d6s30xi\",\"interview_id\":\"vgr4957hkeif\",\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Authentication / Identity / AuthZ, Developer productivity (CLI, codegen, local dev, testing), Payments / billing / entitlements for SaaS\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:11:44\"},{\"id\":\"ywfd8pi1urj5\",\"interview_id\":\"vgr4957hkeif\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"You picked three distinct, heavy categories. Are you building **one unified platform** that spans Auth + DevProd + Billing (like a 'Stripe + Clerk + Vercel CLI' hybrid), or are these separate ideas you're weighing? If it's one product, what's the wedge—the single entry point a developer adopts first?\\\",\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    \\\"Unified platform: Auth is the wedge, then billing, then CLI tooling\\\",\\n    \\\"Unified platform: CLI/DevProd is the wedge, Auth/Billing are add-ons\\\",\\n    \\\"Separate ideas: I'm evaluating which one to pursue\\\",\\n    \\\"It's a meta-framework / boilerplate that wires all three together\\\",\\n    \\\"Something else—let me explain\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"canvas_updates\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_node\\\",\\n      \\\"node\\\": {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"document\\\",\\n        \\\"position\\\": { \\\"x\\\": 300, \\\"y\\\": 250 },\\n        \\\"data\\\": { \\\"label\\\": \\\"Scope Clarification\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"User selected: Auth/Identity, DevProd (CLI/codegen), Payments/Billing. Need to determine if unified or separate.\\\" }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_edge\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"core-concept\\\",\\n      \\\"target\\\": \\\"scope\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:12:08\"},{\"id\":\"cptmfx5kndm6\",\"interview_id\":\"vgr4957hkeif\",\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Unified platform: Auth is the wedge, then billing, then CLI tooling\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:46:26\"},{\"id\":\"zvana2crb9ij\",\"interview_id\":\"vgr4957hkeif\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"question\\\": \\\"Auth as the wedge is smart—it's the first thing every app needs and has high switching costs. But you're entering a bloodbath: Clerk, Auth0, Supabase, Stytch, WorkOS, Firebase, and Ory all own this space. What is your **technical differentiator** at the auth layer that makes a senior engineer say 'I'll migrate to this'? (e.g., fine-grained AuthZ/ReBAC built-in, zero-latency edge sessions, local-first sync, specific compliance, or a radically better local dev story?)\\\",\\n  \\\"options\\\": [\\n    \\\"Fine-grained authorization (ReBAC/SpiceDB-style) built into core, not bolted on\\\",\\n    \\\"True local-first / offline-capable auth with conflict-free sync\\\",\\n    \\\"Edge-native: sub-5ms verification globally via WASM/Workers\\\",\\n    \\\"Developer experience: CLI that spins up full auth+billing+env in seconds locally\\\",\\n    \\\"Open-source core (MIT/Apache) with hosted control plane—no vendor lock-in\\\",\\n    \\\"Compliance-first: SOC2/HIPAA/GDPR primitives baked into schemas\\\",\\n    \\\"Something else—let me explain the technical hook\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"canvas_updates\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_node\\\",\\n      \\\"node\\\": {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"wedge-strategy\\\",\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"document\\\",\\n        \\\"position\\\": { \\\"x\\\": 500, \\\"y\\\": 350 },\\n        \\\"data\\\": { \\\"label\\\": \\\"Wedge Strategy\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Auth → Billing → CLI Tooling\\\" }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_edge\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"core-concept\\\",\\n      \\\"target\\\": \\\"wedge-strategy\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_node\\\",\\n      \\\"node\\\": {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"auth-pillar\\\",\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"document\\\",\\n        \\\"position\\\": { \\\"x\\\": 300, \\\"y\\\": 450 },\\n        \\\"data\\\": { \\\"label\\\": \\\"Auth / Identity\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Core wedge product\\\" }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_edge\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"wedge-strategy\\\",\\n      \\\"target\\\": \\\"auth-pillar\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_node\\\",\\n      \\\"node\\\": {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"billing-pillar\\\",\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"document\\\",\\n        \\\"position\\\": { \\\"x\\\": 500, \\\"y\\\": 450 },\\n        \\\"data\\\": { \\\"label\\\": \\\"Payments / Billing\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Entitlements, subscriptions, usage-based\\\" }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_edge\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"wedge-strategy\\\",\\n      \\\"target\\\": \\\"billing-pillar\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_node\\\",\\n      \\\"node\\\": {\\n        \\\"id\\\": \\\"cli-pillar\\\",\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"document\\\",\\n        \\\"position\\\": { \\\"x\\\": 700, \\\"y\\\": 450 },\\n        \\\"data\\\": { \\\"label\\\": \\\"CLI / Dev Tooling\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Local dev, codegen, testing\\\" }\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"action\\\": \\\"add_edge\\\",\\n      \\\"source\\\": \\\"wedge-strategy\\\",\\n      \\\"target\\\": \\\"cli-pillar\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\",\"created_at\":\"2026-08-03 11:46:57\"}]}"
          },
